# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# This is the whole point of moving off GitHub Pages: any deep route that has no matching
# static file (e.g. /course/<id>/topic/<id>) is served the app shell with an HTTP 200 status
# instead of a 404. Cloudflare Pages serves real static assets first and only applies this
# catch-all when no file matches, so hashed /assets/* and files like /favicon.png are unaffected.
#
# A 200 is what lets Googlebot render the SPA and index public topics. (GitHub Pages serves its
# 404.html fallback with a 404 status, which Google treats as "not found" and never indexes.)
#
# This file must sit at the ROOT of the published directory (dist/). CI copies it there before the
# Cloudflare deploy — see install/cloudflare/README.md.
/*    /index.html    200
